## Why
The scen-check finding is:

- `E2E-001: forbidden verb 'handle' in then`

The product document lists `handle` under `vocabulary.forbidden_actions` with reason "Hides what the program observably does with the input." and replacement "Name the observable action: prints, exits, writes." The `then` step opens with the abstract `handles the name "Ada"` clause and only afterwards names the observable action (`prints "Hello Ada"`). Dropping the abstract clause leaves exactly one observable assertion — the greeter prints `Hello Ada` — which is what the step already asserts; the name `Ada` remains specified by the `when` step (`the Operator runs "greet Ada"`), so no coverage is lost.

Note: the product document declares no `catalogue:`, and this Scenario's `user_stories:` is empty, so no catalogue template constrains the wording of the replacement step.

